{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "Say this to get that. Plain phrases a creator can tap in the Room (Say this tab, Dailies quick asks). Each one becomes a frame-pinned note with the phrase as text. Claude maps the phrase id to the engine action in references/phrasebook.md. `component` = component-kit id (loop file <component>.mp4 in the kit loops folder, ids in kit_ids); `loop` = where a preview loop for a non-kit effect comes from; `preview` stays empty until Claude uploads the loop and writes phrasebook/catalog. `{word}` is filled with the word spoken at the pinned frame. Hero ids (hero_ids) are library heroes: their loops are <hero_loops_dir>/<component>.mp4.",
 "loops_dir": "",
 "groups": [
  {
   "id": "calmer",
   "name": "Calmer",
   "hint": "Too much going on? Take it down."
  },
  {
   "id": "energy",
   "name": "More energy",
   "hint": "Feels flat? Give it a hit."
  },
  {
   "id": "effects",
   "name": "Specific effects",
   "hint": "One effect, on one moment."
  },
  {
   "id": "pacing",
   "name": "Pacing",
   "hint": "Tighter, or room to breathe."
  }
 ],
